Included with the package
-------------------------

census_population_time_series, census_1961_literacy, census_1971, census_1981,
census_subdistricts_2011, census_2011_pca, and the state names used to
harmonise every table derive from:

  Jolad, Shivakumar and Singh, Madhav (2026). Indian Census Data Collection,
  1901-2026: Digitised Subnational Population and Administrative Datasets.
  Harvard Dataverse. doi:10.7910/DVN/ON8CP8. Licensed CC BY 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

The Primary Census Abstract (2001, 2011), C-16 mother tongue and A-10/A-11
Scheduled Caste and Scheduled Tribe tables are published by the Office of the
Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India.

Population projections are published by the Ministry of Health and Family
Welfare, Government of India (state level) and the International Institute
for Population Sciences (district level).

Downloaded on first use
-----------------------

The census boundary files are collated by bharatviz.org from Jolad and Singh
(2026), above, and from https://github.com/ramSeraph/indian_admin_boundaries.
The large 2011 tables and district age projections come from the same
sources as above.
